      "problem": "Evaluate $\\left( \\dfrac{1}{2} + \\sqrt{-9} \\right) + (3 - \\sqrt{-16}).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we simplify the two complex numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{2}+\\sqrt{-9})+(3-\\sqrt{-16}) & =(\\frac{1}{2}+3\\,\\text{i})+(3-4\\,\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo add these two complex numbers, we just add the real parts and add the imaginary parts separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{2}+3\\,\\text{i})+(3-4\\,\\text{i}) & =(\\frac{1}{2}+3)+(3+(-4))\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{2}+3)+(3-4)\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}-1\\,\\text{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{2}-\\,\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
